{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1pjWjsZqd3yt6drn6Na", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off after filing two bugs, both confirmed by the developer. My confidence is about 0.6, because some of the areas were only partly covered.\n\n**Bugs filed**\n- **View mode drops dollar signs.** Money.md contains \"Costs $5 and $10\", but view mode shows \"Costs 5 and 10\".\n- **Regex replace doesn't expand capture groups.** In Regex2.md, searching `(\\w+)@home` with regex on and replacing with `$1-X` gave \"cat@home $1-X\". I expected `$1` to expand to the captured word.\n\n**Checked and working**\n- **Sort:** Reverse order worked with both Size and Name sort, and the setting was kept when I reopened the menu.\n- **Line moves:** Move line up and move line down worked on Indent2.md, and a single undo restored the original order each time.\n- **Duplicate line:** it worked on Single.md, the file with no trailing newline.\n- **View mode:** nested lists in Indent.md and the \"cat@home\" line in Regex.md rendered correctly.\n\n**Not tested**\n- Date and MIME type sort.\n- Rotating the screen.\n- The Zeta folder.\n- Replace all.\n- Whether the step-by-step replace gives the right result when the replacement has no special characters.\n\nI didn't save any edits, so the test files should be unchanged."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 359, "cache_read_input_tokens": 84347, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 359}, "output_tokens": 443, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "265e7b6a-7504-4470-912d-425f4736fb9b", "uuid": "b3966075-144b-4615-9984-b8acec1bc710", "timestamp": "20